\f1\b \cf0 Overview
\f0\b0 \
WAVsToALE generates Avid ALE files from WAV metadata (BEXT, LIST-INFO, embedded XML). It will automatically interpret UCS category & subcatory when files are named with UCS prefixes. And it can infer UCS category/subcategory when no UCS ID prefix is present in the filename.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \

\f1\b Quick Start
\f0\b0 \
1) Open 
\f1\b WAVsToALE.app
\f0\b0 \
2) Choose input WAVs or a folder, and an output directory\
\
4) Click Run; find ALE outputs in your chosen location\
\

\f1\b UCS Inference (Best-Guess)
\f0\b0 \
When filenames lack a UCS ID prefix, the app infers category/subcategory by scoring text from:\
- Filename words\
- BEXT Description\
- LIST-INFO fields\
- Embedded XML text (when present)\
\

\f1\b How scoring works (concise)
\f0\b0 \
- Normalize text (lowercase, strip punctuation, split to words)\
- Score each UCS entry using:\
  - Whole-word overlaps with the UCS Subcategory (highest weight)\
  - Keyword/synonym overlaps from the UCS list (medium weight)\
  - Partial string matches on the Subcategory (lower weight, 3+ chars)\
\
\
